`_process_match_cases` sets `case_list = []` once per tuple `case`, then loops `for element in case` and appends one converted element each time. So immediately before `case_list.append(el)`, the length of `case_list` is just the count of elements already seen in that tuple: 0 on the first iteration, 1 on the second, and so on. The expression `len(case) - 1` is the index of the final element, so it matches `len(case_list)` only on the last iteration of each tuple, not on every evaluation of the append line. Because the suite includes tuples with at least two elements, the relationship fails on earlier iterations and is not an invariant.

